{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1544190-mtaw-dark-eras-origins-of-orders-why-so-late-tome-of-pentacle","id":1544190,"title":"[MtAw Dark Eras] Origins of Orders - Why so late? [Tome of Pentacle]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-10-18T02:43:40-07:00","id":1544190,"title":"[MtAw Dark Eras] Origins of Orders - Why so late? [Tome of Pentacle]","content":"<br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Why do Tome of Pentacle points creation of Diamond Orders so late?</b> Let\u2019s look to canonical events from <b>ToM</b> then.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Pre-Alexander the Great, Awakened are in the desperate cults/covens based on their Great Cults mythos \u2013 but each sharing similarities to 5 general <b><i>Darshanas</i></b> philosophies. With Alexandrian Empire, those desperate cults are mixing, creating <b>constant</b> Darshanas in Awakened circles, firm philosophies groups. And by his death, first <b><i>Tyrannoi</i></b> ( future Seers ) are manipulating Sleepers and Awakened as so called \u2018Diadochi\u2019.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri Light\"><span style=\"color:black\"><b><span style=\"font-size:18px\">ToM Events 1</span></b></span></span><br /> ( All are <b>ToM</b> quotes from page 26-28 )</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>305 BCE:</b> A <b><i>Guardian</i></b> named Admeta discovers the wealthy Eleuisian family she works for founded a secret fellowship that practices mystic rites. Admeta shares her own false occult information and is initiated into the cult, forming the first Labyrinth. ( First Labyrinth in Rome Republic. )</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>295 BCE:</b> The Library of Alexandria is founded. The <b><i>Keepers of the Word</i></b> form with the founding of this first great <b><i>Mouseion</i></b>. (Keepers equivalent of later Atheneum. )</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>270 to 265 BCE:</b> The mages of the Phoenix Brethren build the Adytum of the Mysteries in a Shadow Realm. ( Wyrd\u2019s understanding \u2013 it would probably first canonical greater collection of Pancryptias mages. )</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>218 BCE:</b> While Hannibal crosses the Alps, General-worshiping Diadochi attack a proto-Arrow sanctum; the Arrow is victorious but discovers it was infiltrated \u2014 and the lead proto-Seer is their own Adamant Sage\u2019s brother.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>55 BCE:</b> Roman expedition into Britain encounters Druids. Arrow mages traveling with Caesar obey the Order\u2019s leaders and desert from the army to study the Druids\u2019 magic. When the Romans return and attack the sacred isle of Mona, those same Arrows fight alongside the Druids.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri Light\"><span style=\"color:black\"><b>My question</b></span></span> -</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">So as 55 BCE at most ( and I would even point by 218 BCE ), beside the Silver Ladder proper Convocations \u2013 we <b><i>already</i></b> here have starts of <b><i>Guardians, Arrows, Keepers of the Word </i></b>and <b><i>Panscriptias </i></b>Orders caucuses in Rome or Mediterranean.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">I do not understand <b><i><u>why</u></i></b> <b><i>Silver Ladders</i></b> caucus \u2013 is pointed as created as late as official 265 CE \u2013 <u>almost 500 years later than rest of proto-Orders</u>. <span style=\"font-family:Segoe UI Emoji\">\ud83d\ude32</span> I know (proto-) <b><i>Tearchs</i></b> and <b><i>Tyrannoi </i></b>like to argue in their mixed cults \u2013 but common, they should be created <b><i>at most</i></b> as late as Adamantine Arrow first caucuses! It\u2019s truly puzzling to me. <span style=\"font-family:Segoe UI Emoji\">\ud83e\udd14</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">From the chronicler's duty, the remaining\u2026</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Calibri Light\"><span style=\"color:black\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\">ToM events 2</span> </span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>250 CE:</b> Awakened society is now firmly split between neoplatonists (proto-Diamond) and gnostics (proto-Seers). Relationships between the two sects are hostile.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>265 CE:</b> The first Convocation is held at Alexandria. The Atlantean mages meet and decide to expel Tyrannic cabals, setting down the precepts of the initial Orders and stating that they aren\u2019t part of any Sleeper civilization but draw from all (<i>\u201cThe Awakened are One Nation\u201d</i> \u2014 i.e., the Diamond Precept). The Consilium of Alexandria is disbanded and the Library evacuated for fear of Tyrannic reprisals.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-18-2024, 05:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-18T04:20:42-07:00","id":1544195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1544190-mtaw-dark-eras-origins-of-orders-why-so-late-tome-of-pentacle#post1544190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">( First Labyrinth in Rome Republic. )</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see why you think that. The family being Eleusinian indicates that the family live in Eleusis, ie. Athens. Athens won't be part of the Roman Republic for another 150 years. Also, it's pretty clearly, the origin point for the Labyrinth, not the Guardians. I mean, Admeta is referred to as already being a Guardian before she starts her Labyrinth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">I do not understand <b><i><u>why</u></i></b> <b><i>Silver Ladders</i></b> caucus \u2013 is pointed as created as late as official 265 CE \u2013 <u>almost 500 years later than rest of proto-Orders</u>. <span style=\"font-family:Segoe UI Emoji\">\ud83d\ude32</span> I know (proto-) <b><i>Tearchs</i></b> and <b><i>Tyrannoi </i></b>like to argue in their mixed cults \u2013 but common, they should be created <b><i>at most</i></b> as late as Adamantine Arrow first caucuses! It\u2019s truly puzzling to me. <span style=\"font-family:Segoe UI Emoji\">\ud83e\udd14</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">From the chronicler's duty, the remaining\u2026</span> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure it is pointing to that. Remember that convocations in 2e are an all-Diamond/Pentacle meeting, not just the Silver Ladder. It doesn't necessarily indicate that the Silver Ladder was founded right here. There's presumably a Ladder organisation already extant.<br /> <br /> Also the text says:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Atlantean mages meet and decide to expel Tyrannic cabals, <b>setting down the precepts of the initial Orders</b> and stating that they aren\u2019t part of any Sleeper civilization but draw from all (\u201cThe Awakened are One Nation\u201d \u2014 i.e., the Diamond Precept). </div> </div> </div>You could certainly read that as the Orders being actually founded in 265CE, and that the use of 'Arrow' or 'Guardian' is anachronism for brevity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-18T07:43:56-07:00","id":1544201,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking also about <b>earlier adoption of Draconic Myth</b> - Greeks have myths about dragons from the start. \ud83e\udd14 ( see <i>Hesperid Garden</i> myth ) Other cultures around Mediterranean also. See <b>Scion Dragon</b> for many different stories of Dragons myths, around the world, most much earlier than early Middle Ages and Tremere in Diamond sect ( from 700 CE ). Many times even Draconic myths of culture are from around Bronze Age or earlier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-18-2024, 01:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-18T09:10:58-07:00","id":1544205,"title":"","content":"Organisations can take a long time to coalesce out of philosophy. The Councils of Nicaea, a point considered for a beginning to an actual Christian Church, did not occur until after three hundred years since the life of Christ.<br /> <br /> The Orders coalesce ad hoc over time across the era, but they only become the Diamond when they formally agree to adopt the Silver Ladder's Diamond Precept: &quot;The Awakened are One Nation.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-18T12:01:05-07:00","id":1544216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1544190-mtaw-dark-eras-origins-of-orders-why-so-late-tome-of-pentacle?p=1544201#post1544201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm thinking also about <b>earlier adoption of Draconic Myth</b> - Greeks have myths about dragons from the start. \ud83e\udd14 ( see <i>Hesperid Garden</i> myth ) Other cultures around Mediterranean also. See <b>Scion Dragon</b> for many different stories of Dragons myths, around the world, most much earlier than early Middle Ages and Tremere in Diamond sect ( from 700 CE ). Many times even Draconic myths of culture are from around Bronze Age or earlier.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dragon myths <i>are</i> very old, but they're usually not too positive. The Diamond don't use just any dragon myth. It's the specific identification of the Watchtowers/Oracles with Dragons. In the fully developed Atlantis myth it's that the Dragons are a sort of previously ascended species (maybe).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-18T14:32:59-07:00","id":1544232,"title":"","content":"Mediterranean cultures might have had dragon mythology, but there's no particular reason that the symbolism of such needs to have any prominence to any of the Orders, nor be a feature that arises with significance in the lexicon of their syncretic cultures. There might be an argument that dragons aren't significant enough in any given parent culture of the Diamond as to lend them a lot of clout.<br /> <br /> The big reason to make it an enduring contribution of the Tremere is that it both builds upon what Left-Hand Path introduced about the kinds of dragon symbolism that group emphasizes (which can itself match nicely with the elaboration on their philosophy of hunger), and because it's important <i>that</i> the Tremere make an enduring contribution to the Diamond.<br /> <br /> Like, you could come up with the best argument in the world about why the Orders should be naming themselves after dragon parts and imagining dragons as their precursors in the world, but you'd better come up with some alternative for the legacy of the Tremere while you're at it. And not something shallow or incidental, it needs to be at least as important to the Tremere as the dragon symbolism currently is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-18T18:08:26-07:00","id":1544245,"title":"","content":"For me, Tremere do not <i><b>need</b></i> to bring Dragons - Tremere need to bring <b>SOULS understanding</b> in Awakened circles. They are the ones pointing that Souls are made mostly of Subtle Arcanum and building it whole you need all 5 of them - and something extra in those souls.<br /> <br /> It's also much more important to their dogma - Dragon in their story is just one metaphor. On souls, Tremere thrive and live by, understand them is intrinsic to them. You <i><b>can </b></i><i><b>take out</b></i> easily just Dragon symbols from Tremere stories and still end with souls stealing Liches. You<i><b> cannot take out</b></i> their research on Souls and usage of Souls on general - and still have the same Left-Hand Order the gameline shows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-18T19:01:54-07:00","id":1544247,"title":"","content":"To put something more concrete on topics table - here are my fan notes from 2015 when I analyzed whole 1E Orders books in context of <b>History of Awakened</b> fan project. From what I read in <b>Tome of Pentacle, </b>my guesses from 9 years prior were mostly correct. Only I pointed creation of first Roman Consilium as early as 59 BCE, at most. Then we have 300 years before proper proclamation of Diamond sect in 265 CE in Alexandria. \ud83e\udd14<br /> <br /> I can imagine this working like that - assuming it took about 3 centuries for understanding of new (proto)Orders mages they CANNOT work with Tyrannoi members in those groups. Then in Alexandria 3rd century it's final stroow saying ''no, we will not work with our Tyrannoi ( later Seers ) siblings'. I think it can work like that... \ud83e\udd14<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Wyrd's Fan Timeline</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>264-241 BCE:</b> First Punic War. When Rome and Carthage were fighting on supremacy on Mediterranean Sea, mages joined on both sides of conflict. Members of Adamantine Arrow Darshana fought side by side with Sleepers and against one another. Roman Awakened, as part of Legions, formed tight cult, spreading in all Republic Army. They were one voice, one body and one mind inside Sleepers conflict. And they won with their decentralized half-brothers in Carthage military. ( <b>Fan</b> )<br /> <br /> <b>241 BCE:</b> On the final return to the Italy, first European Caucus of Adamantine Arrow has gathered, from the veterans of this long lasting war. In the shadows of Rome, Arrows sworn to defend the Republic, both Sleepers and Awakened. Keepers of the Word and Pancryptiates already took first steps in the city.( <b>Fan</b> )<br /> <br /> <b>241-218 BCE: </b>Seeing how effective and dangerous newly created Adamantine Arrow Order has become, the local Omphalos Darshana\u2019s cults - worshipping Great Ladder of hierarchy - started to be afraid on their position. For years they infiltrated Roman Senate and elite - so they know vampires had secret nation under the proper Rome. It took almost a decade of debate on what to do with this situation. And then they find out that Phulakeion Darshana - the Guardians called New Constructionist - had infiltrate the Rome and it\u2019s heart - Sanate \u2013 also steering it in to souls prison they though it should be. Finally, Omphalos cult leaders see past their difference and organized a meeting on which they understand they need a strong opposition to both Guardians and Arrows threat. Going after popular Atlantis tale in occult circles, they used Silver Ladder to Heavens as their symbol. From Mantra Sadhaki they taken idea of Supernal Beings \u2013 Dragons \u2013 that teach humanity their true capabilities and role in greater hierarchy of cosmos. First European Silver Ladder Caucus have gathered. After the Kindred they wanted they own, secret nation - but not under the Rome, but <i>inside</i> it. First European Cryptopoly have started. Both Atlantis and Dragon become symbol of Silver Ladder unifying Orders under their Diamond dogma and leading them to recreate utopia in Rome \u2013 even when opposed by both Guardians and vampires in it. ( <b>Guardains of Veil</b> and <b>Fan</b> )<br /> <br /> <b>218-201 BCE:</b> <b>Second Punic War</b>. When Hannibal challenged Rome, almost all of Adamantine Arrow joined Legions in defend of Republic, before his army would crash the Italy. With enemies at their doorstep, occult conflicts were paused. The more armies gone to South, the more inside the Sanate itself the other war was done - free of Arrows watchful eyes, young Silver Ladder were fighting with Guardians over the vision for the Republic. This secret conflict quickly changed idealized forefathers of Tearchs in to power hungry stereotype of Lions that need to much. But the occult war made Guardians into caucus itself, going for every help they could grasp for - using the tools of their brothers in other countries, they started first Roman Labyrinth to gain support. Both new Orders gathered people, influence and backing by proxy of their cults inside Rome\u2019s elite. Keepers of the Word and Pancryptiates do not take active role in this occult conflict, they were strengthening their positions in Rome. ( <b>Fan</b> )<br /> <br /> <b>201-145 BCE: </b>After winning second time with Carthage, and being distracted by other conflict with post-Alexandrian powers, Roman Adamantine Arrow understand it cannot all the time be on war, leaving Rome to other four Orders. They set a part of war veterans as peace keeping guard in the Rome itself, to watch over rest of Awakened and train new recruits. From those the stable Rome\u2019s Arrows caucus have flourished. Rest of the Arrows started to convert they brothers from their own Darshana cults everywhere the Legion went, to fill their ranks on long war campaigns. Other Orders followed this tactics and by the end of Third Punic War all five Orders would become semi-consolidated organizations across whole Empire. Silver Ladder used it\u2019s Atlantis oratory as means to validate it\u2019s rule in governing the unstable alliance to be formed. Roman Republic entered it\u2019s Golden Age with five Diamond Orders the modern mages would easily recognized. ( <b>Fan </b>)<br /> <br /> <b>145 BCE:</b> Ptolemy VIII expelled all foreign scholars from Alexandria, leading to diaspora of <i>Keepers of the Word</i> cult on the Mediterranean Sea area, and becoming of it the proper global Order. ( <b>Fan</b> )<br /> <br /> <b>145-121 BCE: </b>Relative peaceful time bring back much of Adamantine Arrow legionists, with new recruits from conquered region, in flux shaping Awakened community. With growth in all local Orders numbers, mages started power struggles, that also coincidence with start of Sleepers general populace unrests in Rome. ( <b>Fan</b> )<br /> <br /> <b>121-59 BCE: </b>As Rome have new threats of Celts and Germans, Adamantine Arrow started it\u2019s next campaigns and, as a result, introduced next foreign mages to it\u2019s forming ethos. Without Arrows hard supervision, other Diamond Orders start a series of infightings, squabbling over the lead in Roman society. Connected with Sleepers rising problems, Awakened become more ruthless in their study of Mysteries. To end the rising disputes, there is selected first Ruling Council and it\u2019s Hierarch, based on Arcadian Mysteries traditions. First Consilium is officially created. ( <b>Fan</b>, based on the <b>Adamantine Arrow</b> and <b><i>To The Strongest </i></b><b>- Dark Eras</b>)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-19T09:44:04-07:00","id":1544295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1544190-mtaw-dark-eras-origins-of-orders-why-so-late-tome-of-pentacle?p=1544245#post1544245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me, Tremere do not <i><b>need</b></i> to bring Dragons - Tremere need to bring <b>SOULS understanding</b> in Awakened circles. They are the ones pointing that Souls are made mostly of Subtle Arcanum and building it whole you need all 5 of them - and something extra in those souls.</div> </div> </div> </div>But that's just theory. It's not a cultural contribution.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You <i><b>can </b></i><i><b>take out</b></i> easily just Dragon symbols from Tremere stories and still end with souls stealing Liches. You<i><b> cannot take out</b></i> their research on Souls and usage of Souls on general - and still have the same Left-Hand Order the gameline shows.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe, but you'd make them a lot more boring and one-note in the process. I find it akin to a proposition to have the Mysterium without the premise of magic as a living entity. The Orders need to have more than their information to make them feel like something vital and breathing, they need a full range of the quirks and attachments to have a greater sense of depth and praxis.<br /> <br /> If all they needed was souls, there wouldn't have been a drive to build them up away from the corebook portrayal as Left-Hand Path did in the first place. When it was nothing but usage of souls, people were evidently a lot less interested in them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-19T11:06:23-07:00","id":1544301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1544190-mtaw-dark-eras-origins-of-orders-why-so-late-tome-of-pentacle?p=1544247#post1544247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can imagine this working like that - assuming it took about 3 centuries for understanding of new (proto)Orders mages they CANNOT work with Tyrannoi members in those groups. Then in Alexandria 3rd century it's final strow saying ''no, we will not work with our Tyrannoi ( later Seers ) siblings'. I think it can work like that... \ud83e\udd14</div> </div> </div> </div>Expanding my point on Tyrannoi inside proto-Daimond for 325 years, from <b>59 BCE till 265 CE</b> - even <b>Time of Pentacle</b> pointing that later Seers of Throne are deeply submerged in Atlantean culture, using Great Rights even against later Daimond, to 'over-lawing enemies in their own laws'. So first Tyrannoi needed to understand all the culture and laws of Atlanteans. Being over 300 years inside their groups sounds like good starting point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-19-2024, 02:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-19T11:37:00-07:00","id":1544303,"title":"","content":"Other note - taking in account that Diamond is finalized on 265 CE in Alexandria - and Silver Ladder with it on dogma - I would probably run that before, from <b>270 BCE, proto-Diamond is using Darshanas Greek names for themselves</b>, for times being. So we have <i><b>Flakes Tou Logos</b></i> ( Keepers of the Word = Logos ), <i><b>Panscryptias</b></i> - and then <i><b>Omphalos</b></i> ( future Ladder ), <b><i>Phulakeion</i></b> ( Guardians ) and <i><b>Adamnation Velos</b></i> ( Arrows ). Those proto-Orders are starting to be Atlantean in culture, but also having Tyrannoi members. Last Tyranns are finally expelled in 265 CE in Alexandria, with renaming Orders into final Roman names we know today - and finalized split on Diamond and Tyrannoi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-20-2024, 10:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-20T18:41:16-07:00","id":1544369,"title":"","content":"<b>Are the Mages in Origins of Orders era are Literate en masss</b>? Like getting free Merit for that?<br /> <br /> Wikipedia seems to assume that after <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Education_in_ancient_Rome#Ludus\" target=\"_blank\">Ludus and Grammaticus schooling</a>, Romans would be literate to at least run they own books in their workshops. I assume that popular would be taking <b>Language (Greek)</b> as Merit - but not all Romans understood it. On the other hand, Darshanas of that era are clearly Greek inspired in area, so it would be weird for them to not understand Greek language their (proto-)Orders use all the time in concepts. Hmmm... \ud83e\udd14<br /> <br /> <b>So maybe <i>Literate</i> Merit for free, at very least from proto-Orders</b> - but <b>Illiterate</b> as Flaw Condition for those character that are not lucky in their concepts? \ud83e\udd14","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-21-2024, 12:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-20T20:38:24-07:00","id":1544375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1544190-mtaw-dark-eras-origins-of-orders-why-so-late-tome-of-pentacle?p=1544369#post1544369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[B]<br /> <br /> Wikipedia seems to assume that after <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Education_in_ancient_Rome#Schooling\" target=\"_blank\">Ludus and Grammatic us schooling</a>, Romans would be litterate to at least run they own books.</div> </div> </div> </div>How much of that education would farmers get?<br /> <br /> I don't think Awakening necessarily favours the wealthy and educated, and in a world where 90% of everybody is farmers (who are perfectly capable of having encounters with things that might help question the Lie), that's a pretty big target for the Watchtowers to hit. Even if practically speaking I'd imagine that in no point in Awakened history have people that were farmers as Sleepers represented in mage society proportionate to how much of the overall population they were. Just not absent enough to bring assumptions of universal literacy, if that is not to be found among the people the Awakened might have come from.<br /> <br /> If a Dark Era makes literacy into a Merit, I would assume they're approaching from a perspective of it not being a default assumption in society at large, and I see no reason for a mage to assume it as default either. Their apprenticeship might involve being provided with the necessary education, but that &quot;might&quot; is covered in buying the Merit, and its absence can be justified by how the default starting character has not been part of Awakened society long enough to be effectively taught to read.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, I assume that educated and literate ancient mage will endeavour to learn all of the languages of their parent cultures. Greek terminology predominates in To The Strongest because it still would have been the most prominent in Alexander's empire, but the Orders are still founded on the consolidation of Great Cults and the common schools within them from across the Hellenistic world, and that means there's an incentive for the Western Mediterranean mages to learn Persian and Egyptian and at least one Indian language (and maybe some Hebrew in there) as much as the more Eastern ones have to learn Greek and ultimately Latin.<br /> <br /> Never mind everything that should be said about how many Romans would not even have Latin as their native language (even if there become practical and literary reasons to learn it). Some of the centre of what formed the culture of the Diamond Orders shifted towards the Roman Empire as that become the predominant power over that part of the world, but that shouldn't be mistaken for mages becoming heavily central Italian, let alone from or living in the city of Rome. The process of being an empire meant that much of the identifying label of &quot;Roman&quot; flowed out from the centre to become a designation of innumerable different peoples across the provinces, and they in turn returned with expertise and administration and culture. That's how you get several Roman Emperors who came from places like North Africa or Anatolia.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-21T02:00:47-07:00","id":1544380,"title":"","content":"I'm preparing story in <i><b>Origins of Orders</b></i> eras - about creation of permanent Omphalos proto-Order and occult conflict of it inside Senate with New Constructionist Guardians and vampires. I'm preparing high ranking members of <i><b>Omphalos</b></i> - later SL <i><b>Deacon</b></i> equivalent - but we are in 3rd century BCE, so no church tiltes are there to use. How to call those high ranking Omphalos? Go with vampires route - and call the Augures? \ud83e\udd14 Other ideas?<br /> <br /> Beside that - I was thinking about calling them <b><i>Exarch</i></b>, just to play on the nose that Omphalos is still full of Tyrannoi inside. \ud83d\ude08 However, Exarchat name is also from 4th century Byzantine church title.<br /> <br /> I also thought about names for future called Exarchs beings - I then thought that a lot of Arcadian Mysteries is based on calling the <i><b>Olympian</b></i> gods for help - so maybe use them in place of future Exarchs names<br /> <br /> Death - Hades<br /> Fate - Hera? Moiras?<br /> Forces - Zeus<br /> Life - Demeter / Dionizos<br /> Matter - Hephaestus<br /> Mind - Athena<br /> Prime - Hecate(?)<br /> Space - Hermes<br /> Spirit - Gaia<br /> Time - Chronos?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-27-2024, 12:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-21T05:46:48-07:00","id":1544387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1544190-mtaw-dark-eras-origins-of-orders-why-so-late-tome-of-pentacle?p=1544380#post1544380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Beside that - I was thinking about calling them <b><i>Exarch</i></b>, just to play on the nose that Omphalos is still full of Tyrannoi inside. \ud83d\ude08 However, Exarchat name is also from 4th century Byzantine church title.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Exarch&quot; is preceded in its use as a term for a rank in the Eastern Orthodox Church by being a secular title for provincial governors used by the Eastern Roman Empire.<br /> <br /> It's also just a Greek word derived from the roots &quot;eks&quot; (from outside) and &quot;archon&quot; (ruler). I think it's likely that there were many scenarios in which it would have been used informally; as a way to describe another city with supremacy over yours, for instance. After conquest, there may even have been Greeks who used it as a term for Romans.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-21T06:16:49-07:00","id":1544389,"title":"","content":"Wyrd why even ask the question if you're gonna vehemently brush aside answers and just posit an alternate history you've obviously put work into?<br /> <br /> Just make the thread about your alternate history at that point","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-21T06:29:30-07:00","id":1544390,"title":"","content":"Wyrd why even ask the question if you're gonna vehemently brush aside answers and just posit an alternate history you've obviously put work into?<br /> <br /> Just make the thread about your alternate history at that point","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-21T06:29:30-07:00","id":1544391,"title":"","content":"Wyrd why even ask the question if you're gonna vehemently brush aside answers and just posit an alternate history you've obviously put work into?<br /> <br /> Just make the thread about your alternate history at that point","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-21T08:18:07-07:00","id":1544398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1544190-mtaw-dark-eras-origins-of-orders-why-so-late-tome-of-pentacle?p=1544387#post1544387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's also just a Greek word derived from the roots &quot;eks&quot; (from outside) and &quot;archon&quot; (ruler). </div> </div> </div> </div>Using then 'Exarchon' as title equivalent of Deacon in Omphalos cults? Or maybe simply 'Archon'?\ud83e\udd14<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-21T10:00:47-07:00","id":1544403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1544190-mtaw-dark-eras-origins-of-orders-why-so-late-tome-of-pentacle?p=1544398#post1544398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Using then 'Exarchon' as title equivalent of Deacon in Omphalos cults? Or maybe simply 'Archon'?\ud83e\udd14<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say the former would be functional enough; it can imply something about the occult nature of their guidance, the separation between them and their Cryptopolies, while still having that allusion to the future. Archon has the advantage of being more straightforward and blunt.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, one could follow the trend of things like the Path names and give them an earlier Greek version of the same title; the word deacon derives from the ancient Greek &quot;diakonos&quot;, meaning servant, minister, or messenger.<br /> <br /> Or, if there's a desire to make Roman terms more prominent, one could go direct to pontifex. Indeed, you brought up augurs before, and if you'd want to emphasize that there's still a struggle with early Exarch cultists, one could have <i>both</i> terms in use for the upper ranks of the Order, drawing on the symbolism or lexicon of the society they're nested within (as augurs were a separate religious college from pontiffs), where the choice in title arises from what one sees as the main function of their role.<br /> <br /> Indeed, pontifex is proposed to have an etymology in which it derives from Latin words meaning &quot;bridge builder&quot;, which those mages might see as referring to the role of building the great ladder of being, compared to those who dig in searching for signs and portents from on high.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-23T00:36:25-07:00","id":1544537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1544190-mtaw-dark-eras-origins-of-orders-why-so-late-tome-of-pentacle?p=1544387#post1544387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's also just a Greek word derived from the roots &quot;eks&quot; (from outside) and &quot;archon&quot; (ruler).</div> </div> </div> </div>I always wondered why the original writers went for 'exarch' and not 'archon'. That's actually quite clever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-23T06:38:15-07:00","id":1544547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1544190-mtaw-dark-eras-origins-of-orders-why-so-late-tome-of-pentacle?p=1544537#post1544537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I always wondered why the original writers went for 'exarch' and not 'archon'. That's actually quite clever.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect also a general intention to be less on the nose with the Gnostic influences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-24T03:23:22-07:00","id":1544637,"title":"","content":"My player want to bring <b>Tamer of Fire </b>to our Rome Senate adventure, in heart of Sanate. I'm all for the Legacy itself - but it's history is a bit problematic, especially in 2E history take. <b>Elemental Masteries</b> are to rise from 'fallen era civilisations', however they tried to join 'Dragon Orders' and 'was not meet with opened hands'. How would Darshanas and protoOrders of 3rd century see the <b>Tamers</b> on general? \ud83e\udd14","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-24T14:08:45-07:00","id":1544682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1544190-mtaw-dark-eras-origins-of-orders-why-so-late-tome-of-pentacle?p=1544637#post1544637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My player want to bring <b>Tamer of Fire </b>to our Rome Senate adventure, in heart of Sanate. I'm all for the Legacy itself - but it's history is a bit problematic, especially in 2E history take. <b>Elemental Masteries</b> are to rise from 'fallen era civilisations', however they tried to join 'Dragon Orders' and 'was not meet with opened hands'. How would Darshanas and protoOrders of 3rd century see the <b>Tamers</b> on general? \ud83e\udd14</div> </div> </div> </div>Suspicion at best (&quot;maybe he is a spy&quot;) or skepticism at worst (&quot;he just talks to fire and it listens&quot;). Given how the senate includes great orators and leaders, it would also give them a great opportunity to gain prestige with their skill at rhetoric, which would help build the Legacy's reputation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-25T03:08:46-07:00","id":1544713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1544190-mtaw-dark-eras-origins-of-orders-why-so-late-tome-of-pentacle?p=1544637#post1544637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would Darshanas and protoOrders of 3rd century see the <b>Tamers</b> on general? \ud83e\udd14</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a good question, but not one that we really have a clear answer for. There are a smattering of references to the Tamers still being on the outs of mage society, but why exactly isn't really made clear.<br /> <br /> Like, the 2e core says that they're &quot;perhaps the oldest legacies in the Fallen World&quot;, however you'll note that they don't appear in <i>The Sundered World</i>... Further, their elemental schema is literally the one that the mage societies of <i>To the Strongest</i> use... It's specifically the classical elements of Aristotle. Honestly, without their history as non-Atlantean mages, the Tamers being separate from the Darshanas doesn't feel all that coherent. In your situation I would be tempted to just ditch the animosity and have them as accepted legacies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-25T08:49:01-07:00","id":1544727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1544190-mtaw-dark-eras-origins-of-orders-why-so-late-tome-of-pentacle?p=1544713#post1544713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like, the 2e core says that they're &quot;perhaps the oldest legacies in the Fallen World&quot;, however you'll note that they don't appear in <i>The Sundered World</i>...</div> </div> </div> </div>Even apart from questions of whether or not that was deemed worth including compared to more new stuff with limited wordcount, The Sundered World can hardly be the entirety of Awakened in the Neolithic (and I recall contains language to the extent of making that explicit).<br /> <br /> It's an important location because it's where they opt to place the actual preamble of the Sundering (and because of the developer's personal fascination with drawing on such a material culture), but there are still other cultural contexts in existence at the time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Further, their elemental schema is literally the one that the mage societies of <i>To the Strongest</i> use</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's at least reminiscent of the names given for the ancient versions of the Paths.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure it quite fits under classical elements if it's not contending that they're the sum composition of everything in existence. Even Aristotle could be argued to be creating that schema out of older categorisations based on the fact that things like water, wind, and fire are quite evident and evocative. There's evidence of them as specific motifs going back far further than about 2500 years. That's before bringing in something like &quot;Cave&quot; as an element. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">without their history as non-Atlantean mages, the Tamers being separate from the Darshanas doesn't feel all that coherent. In your situation I would be tempted to just ditch the animosity and have them as accepted legacies.</div> </div> </div> </div>But then where does the line fall between magical traditions that coalesce into the Diamond Orders and ones that become Nameless for almost two thousand years?<br /> <br /> I think if the Tamers are being described as something that extends far into the past, they should be attributed the kind of philosophy developed to the point where they would not agree with the Atlantean praxis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-25T09:11:27-07:00","id":1544731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1544190-mtaw-dark-eras-origins-of-orders-why-so-late-tome-of-pentacle?p=1544713#post1544713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">iterally the one that the mage societies of <i>To the Strongest</i> use... It's specifically the classical elements of Aristotle. Honestly, without their history as non-Atlantean mages, the Tamers being separate from the Darshanas doesn't feel all that coherent. In your situation I would be tempted to just ditch the animosity and have them as accepted legacies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it's also I see:<br /> <br /> 1. <b>Tamers Elements</b> are literal Path associations of Paths from <i>To the Strongest</i> era.<br /> 2. Adding Atlantis myth later on, in Atlantean sects ( proto-Diamond ) after Plato published works in 360 BCE, makes it weird that Tamers are 'some special mages cult group' to be ousted.<br /> <br /> Like, Tamers maybe not work like direct 5 Darshanas of future Diamond ( priest-, warriors-, researchers-, infiltrators- and 'living'-mages ) - Tamers have their own Darshana-like structure.<br /> <br /> HOWEVER, I could make Tamers to be stoping forces for Diamond coalescence - being antagonists to Darshana model unification? \ud83e\udd14 But it's a bit fruitless, and maybe really unnecessary from gameplay reasons<br /> <br /> Maybe just go with (proto)<b><i>Diamond stand on Tamers </i></b>as <i>'they don't work with our 5 Greate Castes model, they are weird - but this Elemental magic is cool' </i>? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-25-2024, 12:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}